# `.env.*` above matches `.env.example` too, and that file is documentation, not
# a secret: it is the only record in the repo of the eleven VITE_* variables the
# build needs, since `.env.local` is ignored. It survived for a long time only
# because it was tracked before the `.env.*` rule existed — so once anything
# removes it from the index it becomes invisible to `git add -A` and silently
# stops being committed. This negation is what keeps it tracked.
!.env.example
.DS_Store
.claude/
lint_output.txt

